cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this simulator, please cite it as below."
title: "Space Debris Capture Simulator: tumbling 12U CubeSat captured by a Kevlar 49 net"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/euparth/SpaceRobotsMS"
url: "https://space-debris-sim.vercel.app"
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Parth
    email: euparth@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Browser-based simulator of a non-cooperative tumbling 12U CubeSat (Ix = 0.479, Iy = 0.273,
  Iz = 0.464 kg·m², z intermediate) captured by a 2 × 2 m tension-only XPBD net. Torque-free
  Euler equations integrated with RK4 at H = 1/3000 s in a Web Worker; closed-form spin-envelope
  criterion for the fire-now decision; seeded in-browser Monte Carlo over spin priors that
  reproduces the committed dataset; MLP surrogate retained for comparison; verification and
  limitations on the /methods page. The 2023 M.Sc. thesis of the author (TH OWL) reviewed Shin
  et al.'s ABAQUS net-capture study; this simulator is an independent re-implementation of that
  scenario.
keywords:
  - space debris
  - net capture
  - rigid-body dynamics
  - intermediate-axis instability
  - XPBD
  - CubeSat
